/*
Problem: Minimum Distance Between BST Nodes (LC 783)
Topic: Binary Search Tree / Inorder Traversal

--------------------------------------------------

Idea:

Inorder traversal of a BST visits
nodes in sorted order.

Therefore, the minimum difference can
only occur between two consecutive
nodes in this sorted sequence.

Keep track of the previously visited
node and compute the difference with
the current node.

--------------------------------------------------

Algorithm:

1. Perform inorder traversal.

2. Traverse the left subtree.

3. If a previous node exists:

   Update the minimum difference.

4. Update the previous node to the
   current node.

5. Traverse the right subtree.

6. Return the minimum difference.

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

      4
     / \
    2   6
   / \
  1   3

Inorder:

1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 6

Differences:

1, 1, 1, 2

Answer:

1

--------------------------------------------------

Example:

Input:

      1
       \
        3
       /
      2

Inorder:

1 → 2 → 3

Differences:

1, 1

Answer:

1

--------------------------------------------------

Why It Works?

Inorder traversal of a BST produces
values in ascending order.

Hence, the smallest difference must
be between adjacent values in this
sorted order.

--------------------------------------------------

Time : O(n)

Every node is visited once.

Space : O(h)

h = Height of the tree due to the
recursion stack.

Worst case: O(n)

--------------------------------------------------

Pattern:

Binary Search Tree / Inorder Traversal
*/

class Solution {
public:

    TreeNode* prev = NULL;

    int minDiffInBST(TreeNode* root) {

        int ans = INT_MAX;

        if (root == NULL)
            return INT_MAX;

        // Traverse left subtree
        if (root->left) {

            int leftMin =
                minDiffInBST(root->left);

            ans = min(ans, leftMin);
        }

        // Compare with previous node
        if (prev != NULL) {

            ans = min(ans,
                      root->val - prev->val);
        }

        // Update previous node
        prev = root;

        // Traverse right subtree
        if (root->right) {

            int rightMin =
                minDiffInBST(root->right);

            ans = min(ans, rightMin);
        }

        return ans;
    }
};
